  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently, the way of syncing animations on your avatar with everyone else is by driving synced parameters with \"Local Only\" Parameter Drivers. This is great, however there can be a lot of latency involved when a remote player sends an interaction to you, you update your synced parameter, and send it back to them. This makes anything time-sensitive almost impossible. My proposal is a \"Sync remote to local\" parameter driver, that updates the local player's synced parameters. This shifts the latency from the interacting player, to the local player/other remote players.",
